    "text": "The bar chart compares the proportions of residents cycling each week in North and South in 2010, 2015 and 2020. All figures are expressed as percentages.\n\nOverall, the proportion in North increased overall, whereas South decreased overall. North recorded the higher figure at the end of the period. The difference between the regions narrowed, from 35 percentage points in 2010 to 20 points in 2020.\n\nIn North, the figure stood at 29% in 2010, before rising to 34% five years later. It then increased to 69% in 2020. The first interval saw a change of 5 percentage points, while the corresponding movement during the second half of the decade was 35 points.\n\nSouth followed a different pattern, starting at 64% and reaching 59% in 2015. By 2020, its figure was 49%. Comparing the two regions directly, South had the larger share at the beginning, while North led at the end. The final figures of 69% for North and 49% for South therefore show a gap of 20 percentage points.",
